<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piet Cronjé</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a>–<a href="/years/1911">1911</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pieter Arnoldus Cronjé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piet Cronjé was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> general of the South African Republic. He forced the surrender of the Jameson raiders in January 1896 and, in the Second Boer War, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahikeng">Mafeking</a> and defeated the British at Magersfontein in December 1899. Trapped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-roberts-1st-earl-roberts">Lord Roberts</a> at Paardeberg, he surrendered with about 4,000 men on 27 February 1900 and was held as a prisoner of war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piet-cronje.jpg" alt="Piet Cronjé" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B. Grant · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PACronje_CHM_VA2863.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
